# What ships from this folder is exactly what a player needs to RUN the game:
#   game.exe, the runtime DLLs, and the asset folders (models/ maps/ shaders/ textures/).
# Everything else is a local build/dev artifact and is excluded here. Adding a file to this
# list is not enough on its own if it was already committed - it must also be untracked with
# `git rm --cached <path>`, because .gitignore has no effect on files git is already tracking.

# --- Diagnostics. Every log, dump and self-test report goes to logs/ (see src/LogPath.h,
# logpath::of). The loose entries below are pre-logpath artifacts that must not come back.
logs/
*.log
*.dmp
ClaudeRTS-log*.txt
ClaudeRTS-crash.txt
coll_debug.txt
route_debug.txt
routeguard.txt
routedetach.txt
routegpu_selftest.txt
perframe_*.log

# --- Dev/test tooling. Useful locally, not part of a client install.
*.bat
game.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.lib

# --- Editor DATA. These are BAKED into game.exe (EmbeddedEditorData.inc) and getEditorText()
# prefers a loose file over the embed - so a shipped copy silently OVERRIDES the build's own
# data. build.bat deletes them from this folder after every deploy; this keeps a stray one
# that appears between builds (a client run re-saves them) from ever being committed.
albedo_overrides.txt
bot_order.txt
cluster_templates.txt
construction.txt
custom_categories.txt
effects.txt
map_order.txt
mesh_variants.txt
model_overrides.txt
model_src_overrides.txt
overrides.txt
print_shapes.txt
production.txt
props.txt
render_settings.txt
resource_effects.txt
start_config.txt
submesh_materials.txt
team_masks.txt
tuning.txt
walk_states.txt

# config.txt is the ONE data file that stays local rather than shipping: it holds this
# machine's window/camera prefs, which the game writes itself and no other machine wants.
config.txt

# --- Mesh cache: rebuilt by the game from models/ on first run (GB-scale .mbin files, well
# over GitHub's 100 MB/file limit). Anyone who runs the game regenerates their own.
meshcache/
*.mbin

# --- Icon PNGs are human-readable PREVIEWS only. The game loads icons from textures/*.rgba;
# these come from `game.exe dumpicons <dir>` and have no runtime use.
icons/
icon_previews/

# --- Backup copies kept beside the folder rather than in it.
_ucrt-backup/
